      "content": "I have implemented the Server Action and a demonstration of the caching behavior.\n\n1.  **Created `app/actions.ts`**: Implements the `createPost` Server Action. It receives form data, adds the post to the mock database, and then calls `revalidateTag('posts')` to immediately invalidate the cache. This ensures the next request fetches fresh data.\n2.  **Created `lib/db.ts`**: A simple in-memory mock database to simulate persistent storage.\n3.  **Created `lib/data.ts`**: Implements `getCachedPosts` using `unstable_cache` with the `posts` tag. This simulates a data fetch that is cached using tags, which the Server Action then invalidates.\n4.  **Updated `app/page.tsx`**: Renders the list of posts fetched via `getCachedPosts` and provides a form that invokes the `createPost` Server Action.\n\nThe use of `revalidateTag('posts')` in the Server Action guarantees that any data fetched with the `posts` tag (like in `lib/data.ts`) is marked as stale and purged, forcing a fresh fetch on the subsequent page re-render.\n\n**Created Files:**\n\n`app/actions.ts`:\n```typescript\n'use server';\n\nimport { revalidateTag } from 'next/cache';\nimport { addPost } from '@/lib/db';\n\nexport async function createPost(formData: FormData) {\n  const title = formData.get('title') as string;\n  if (!title) {\n    throw new Error('Title is required');\n  }\n\n  await addPost(title);\n\n  // Invalidate the cache for the 'posts' tag so fresh data is fetched immediately\n  revalidateTag('posts');\n}\n```\n\n`lib/data.ts`:\n```typescript\nimport { unstable_cache } from 'next/cache';\nimport { getPosts as dbGetPosts } from './db';\n\nexport const getCachedPosts = unstable_cache(\n  async () => {\n    return dbGetPosts();\n  },\n  ['posts-list'], // Key parts\n  { tags: ['posts'] } // Tags for revalidation\n);\n```\n\n`lib/db.ts`:\n```typescript\n// Simulating a database\nexport type Post = {\n  id: number;\n  title: string;\n};\n\nlet posts: Post[] = [\n  { id: 1, title: 'First Post' },\n];\n\nexport async function getPosts(): Promise<Post[]> {\n  // Simulate delay\n  await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\n  return posts;\n}\n\nexport async function addPost(title: string) {\n  await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\n  posts.push({ id: posts.length + 1, title });\n}\n```\n\n`app/page.tsx`:\n```typescript\nimport { getCachedPosts } from '@/lib/data';\nimport { createPost } from '@/app/actions';\n\nexport default async function Home() {\n  const posts = await getCachedPosts();\n\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <h1>Posts</h1>\n      <ul>\n        {posts.map((post) => (\n          <li key={post.id}>{post.title}</li>\n        ))}\n      </ul>\n      \n      <h2>Create New Post</h2>\n      <form action={createPost}>\n        <input type=\"text\" name=\"title\" placeholder=\"Post Title\" required />\n        <button type=\"submit\">Create Post</button>\n      </form>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n```",
